  "name": "Reese Drift",
  "author": "Riddim Rack",
  "description": "Detuned reese: Saw Stack in 6-voice unison (22 cents, width 0.6) on Osc A plus a 5-voice Saw Stack 7 cents sharp on Osc B, spread A left / B right, both through LP12s that the filter envelope sweeps open over about a second, a clean sine sub at the played pitch underneath and everything mono below 120 Hz. Play: long notes and slides around F1-C2 (halftime, DnB); overlap notes for legato glides. Tweak: Osc A/B Detune for the beating speed, Filter Env Amt and Decay for the sweep, Spread and Width for stereo size, Sub Level for weight. Macro plan (not wired yet): Detune = Osc A + B Detune, Sweep = Filter Env Amt, Width = unison Width + Spread, Weight = Sub Level.",
